WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.502
-So I want to start with this.
You are, obviously, in a very --

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:05.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
reporting on a very difficult
story right now.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.306 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You're very composed.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:09.876
And, yet, I heard on your way
out here, you were at LAX.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.311 line:92%
And you lost your composure.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You heard about this?
-Yes.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I ran into Joe Biden.
-Right.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:15.415 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-So the backstory is --

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:18.418
first of all, Joe Biden is like
sitting by himself at LAX,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.486 line:92%
by himself, 100% by himself,

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
wearing the aviators
in the corner.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"That's Joe Biden."

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.458
-So, I'm like, "I got to go talk
to Joe Biden."

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:29.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
The backstory is my
father-in-law in 1987-88

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
worked on
his presidential campaign.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They were close.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.034
My wife told me, "We hung out
with the Biden kids a lot,

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:34.701 size:81% position:41% line:92%
like, great memories."

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm like, "I got to go
tell him this."

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.937 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So I go up to Joe Biden.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:42.375
I say, "Hey, Mr. Vice President,
I'm Jacob Soboroff from MSNBC.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you?"

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.811 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Hey, great to see you."

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.046 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So then I got nervous.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said to him,
"My daughter --"

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have a daughter.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.153 line:92%
"i-is my father-in-law's wife."

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like -- and then
I said it again.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.360
I was like, "My daughter is
my father-in-law's wife."

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.561 line:92%
And he wasn't responding.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.930 size:78% position:39%
And he kind of, like,
takes the aviators.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he looks over.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh,
my wife is my wife.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.600 size:78% position:39%
And my father-in-law
is my father-in-law."

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Oh, how are they?
Tell them I said hello."

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I'm sorry,
Mr. Vice President,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.073 line:92%
if you're watching tonight.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:13.740 line:92%
I'll never do that again.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's like
you were asking him a riddle.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was bad.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.545 line:92%
I was very uncomfortable.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My wife is my daughter-in-law
is my father.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
So who's the doctor?
-Exactly.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.018 line:92%
-So you actually had been doing,

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.587
even before the family
separation policy went in place,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had been doing a wonderful
piece about the border.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you've been down there.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:35.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you actually spent time
on every mile

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.663 line:92%
of the U.S./Mexico border.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-2,000 miles, yeah.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.465 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Which is incredible.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you, of course, I think we
all have this image of

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
the border based on
the news reporting we see.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually went down there
and saw a different story

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the sort of
outrageous things

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.111 line:92%
we hear every day on the news.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.880
-It really is unbelievable to me
to hear about how people,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.649
particularly the President,
talk about what is going on

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:00.553
down on the border as if it is
just the most lawless crazy area

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.254 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you have ever been to.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.457
It's some of the most wonderful
people I've ever met

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.059 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in my entire life.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of the safest cities
in America

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.761 line:92%
are along the southern border.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.831
The idea that drugs are flowing
in where there's no wall

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:12.565 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is factually incorrect.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.767
If the President took some time
to read his own DEA reports,

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.770
he would know that violence is
not flowing across the border.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
He would know that
drugs are coming in

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.740 line:92%
through legal ports of entry.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.210
And he would know that MS-13 is
a tiny, tiny, tiny, tiny percent

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.178 line:92%
of the people that come through.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the poli-- I mean,
basically they make policies

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
that rip children away from
their families

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
and are truly ripping apart
the fabric of society

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.453 size:75% position:38% line:92%
based on a nonsense.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:37.790
-Now, you actually, you mention
you met great people.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.194
This was -- This is a true thing
that happened.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.395 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Explain what happened.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.364 line:92%
But this is a man who saw you.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He swam across to you
to offer you...

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shrimp.
-Shrimp.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.304 line:92%
-So, this is the Rio Grande,

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the Rio Grande
meets the Gulf of Mexico.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:58.077
And that's the very southeastern
most point of the U.S. border.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.546 line:92%
And this guy calls across to me.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:02.482 size:88% position:44%
He's like, "Hey, buddy."
And I was like, "Hey."

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:05.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like,
"Do you want some shrimp?"

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.720
And I said, "Yeah, come across.
I'll take some shrimp."

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.758
So the guy --
In that cooler also were limes.

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there -- That's
the hot sauce right there.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so for 5 bucks,
the whole thing,

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.096 line:92%
with the militarized border

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just all this divisive
sort of things,

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.967
the guy swam across and just
blew my mind about everything

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.870
that we -- you know, you think
you know about what is going on.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I thank this man very much.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was delicious.
-Well, that -- yeah.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.776 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:34.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you never --
I never once heard Trump say,

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.515 line:92%
"They're sending their shrimp."

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no shrimp.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:37.850 line:92%
-So you mentioned that the drugs

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
are actually coming through
the ports of entry that exist.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:45.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Based on that, is what
you're saying that a wall,

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
while, you know,
sort of as a symbol,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.295 line:92%
seems like a show of strength,

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
would not actually fix
any of the problems right now

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.367 line:92%
as far as the drug trade goes.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, no.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.303 size:84% position:42%
And people shouldn't be
surprised when they --

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.271 line:92%
the President knows this.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's in the DEA reports
that he gets.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.442 size:84% position:42%
And he continues to say
over and over again.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:05.445
By the way, it also is not gonna
stop the vast majority of people

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are coming to
this country illegally.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.582
The majority of people that come
into the country illegally

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:13.653
fly here from Asia, for the most
part, and overstay their visas.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.423
And no wall is going to stop
people flying in, you know,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.325 size:78% position:39% line:92%
obviously, from Asia.

